        "id": "s163-pixel-topology",
        "description": "One source subfigure. Right-isosceles triangle with upper apex and horizontal base. Two parallel rays enter from the left on the sloping face at different heights. Upper ray 1 slopes down-right to a base reflection on the right half, then up-right and leaves at the lower height. Lower ray 2 slopes down-right to a base reflection on the left half, then up-right and leaves at the upper height. Their internal paths cross (not a branch or a third ray). Both output rays still travel rightward. No angle numbers or point names; four labels are left upper 1, left lower 2, right upper 2, right lower 1. Glass hatching becomes neutral fill. Tiny vertex/contact anchors are modern additions, not source dot glyphs.",
